# Shoehorning against licensing (2026-10-07)

**Outputs:** `<full run folder>/licensing_analysis_2026-10-07_03-35/` (script `scripts/shoehorning_audit/analyze_shoehorning_against_licensing.py`). Licensing rules are the plan's "Licensed by" lines, matched to exact variable strings (`licensing_table_*.csv`); per document and item the status is licensed > partly licensed > unlicensed. "Shoehorned" = the document has a staged or unmotivated occurrence of the item. Numbers below come from `most_frequently_shoehorned_items_*.csv`, `items_most_likely_shoehorned_when_present_*.csv`, `shoehorning_by_licensing_status_*.csv` and `unlicensed_items_by_resolution_kind_*.csv`; Wilson intervals are in the CSVs.

